{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PlanarEmbedding","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"G","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"G","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Graph","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A self-loop appears twice in its vertex’s order, its two ends adjacent, enclosing a face of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"length 1. Parallel copies sit side by side, each consecutive pair enclosing a face of length 2."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Each clockwise order starts at the first edge of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentEdges(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Faces.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" The face after the half-edge from u along edge e to w continues with the half-edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"before e in the clockwise order at w (NetworkX’s "},{"code":"next_face_half_edge","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), so a face lies to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"right of each of its half-edges. Faces are counted per connected component, and an isolated"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex has none: two disjoint triangles have four faces."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The embedding keeps the graph it was made from (copy-on-write, so O(1)); mutating the graph"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"afterwards does not change it. When a graph has several embeddings, which one is returned is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not specified, but it depends only on the graph’s rows: graphs with the same vertices, the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edge positions and the same incidence order get the same embedding."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/PlanarEmbedding"},"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Planarity\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/Planarity\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/Planarity\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/Planarity\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Planarity\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo"}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Structures","generated":true,"anchor":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/PlanarEmbedding\/ClockwiseIncidentEdges","doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/PlanarEmbedding\/ClockwiseNeighborIndices","doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/PlanarEmbedding\/ClockwiseNeighbors","doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/PlanarEmbedding\/Faces-swift.struct"]},{"title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/PlanarEmbedding\/faceCount","doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/PlanarEmbedding\/faces-swift.property"]},{"title":"Instance Methods","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/PlanarEmbedding\/clockwiseIncidentEdges(of:)","doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/PlanarEmbedding\/clockwiseIncidentEdges(safe:)","doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/PlanarEmbedding\/clockwiseNeighborIndices(ofIndex:)","doc:\/\/Planarity\/